"Full rules as directed (2026-08-14):\n1. OWNERSHIP: a generated map instance is reused only by the player who caused its generation — mark the instance with its player (future: its party). Today activation already generates one instance per locationless player; this makes that intentional and durable instead of incidental.\n2. PATH ROUTING: because instances are per-player, one authored cross-map path may need to send different players to different destination instances — destination resolution becomes (connection, traveling player) -> instance, not connection -> instance.\n3. COMMON ZONES: maps explicitly designated common (e.g. towns) are shared. A new instance of a common zone is generated only when every previous instance has an excessive player count — heuristic cap: more than 1 player per room of the area.\n4. PARTY OVERRIDE: if anyone in your party is already in a common zone instance, you join them regardless of the cap. Being in a party side-steps ALL new-zone-generation rules; you are simply placed with your party members.\n5. PARTY ENTITY: party is an abstract entity existing only as a unique pointer for players' party components. Party-specific components may attach to it later if party state is ever needed; none are planned now."